# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Added here: Vahlarriel's Vengeance (97284), on the Thunder Axe Fortress visit; The Karnitol Shipwreck (1454, 1455) and the
# satchel's errand (1456), whose chest lies by Azore's tower on the way to the fortress; Carved Centaur Totems (93224),
# whose totems the Kolkar drop with Centaur Bounty's ears (#1602; 30-40/06b keeps it for a player who loads it fresh).
# Left out: Bodyguard for Hire (5821).
# Since 2026-11-07 this first Desolace visit comes after Stranglethorn's first loop (33-35); the south loop stays at
# the end of 30-40, in 30-40/06b-desolace (38-39), which dives for Karnitol's satchel on its north-west coast.
# Since the 2026-11-20 fix round Claim Rackmore's Treasure! (6161) is done here: its log lies beside Karnitol's Chest,
# the silver key drops from the Drysnap crabs around the wreck (33-35), the golden key from the Slitherblade naga of
# the coast north of it (32-35) and the chest stands at the coast's northern tip, so the coast is walked once, north
# from the wreck and back south-east past Azore's tower to Thunder Axe Fortress (about 1,400 yards added). Bone
# Collector (5501) is taken at Kormek's Hut on the way from the fortress to Smeed's camp, its Kodo Bones lie in the
# graveyard the kodo taming already works, and Bibbly takes them on the way home from Kolkar Village. Both were carried
# to the south loop at 38-39 before. Left there: Karnitol's satchel (1456), which Kreldig gives only on the last
# Nijel's Point stop and which drops from the Tidehunters and Sea Witches (35-37), and the Book of the Ancients (6027),
# whose Lord Kragaru (38) rises at the Serpent Statue: Azore gives it when the Sceptre of Light (5741, level 33) is
# handed in, which is done here, back up his hill from the fortress (about 1,600 yards added; it rode five guides to
# the south loop before), and it is carried there. Highway Robbery (79229) starts at an Extinguished
# Campfire just north of the Kodo Bones, goes to Bibbly at Kormek's Hut on the way home, and Bibbly's On the Lam
# (79235) is carried to Tokal at the end of 30-40/04b in Booty Bay (about 200 yards added).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Getting there

step Nijel's Point
  zone Desolace
  tip Follow the road west past Sun Rock Retreat (Horde) and south-west through the Charred Vale into Desolace; Nijel's Point stands at the top of the pass.
  getfp "Nijel's Point" npc 6706      -- Baritanas Skyriver
  sethome "Nijel's Point" npc 11103   -- Innkeeper Lyshaerya
  turnin 1453                         -- Kreldig Ungor
  accept 1458
  accept 1454                         -- Kreldig Ungor: the wreck's chest lies below Azore's tower, on the way to Thunder Axe Fortress
  accept 1437                         -- Vahlarriel Demonslayer

step Malem chest
  tip The chest lies in the ruins south-west of Nijel's Point.
  turnin 1437                         -- Malem Chest
  accept 1465

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- North-east

step Sargeron
  tip The Hatefury satyrs hold the ruins of Sargeron, east of Nijel's Point.
  tip Careful: Hatefury Rogues spawn stealthed, and Hatefury Tricksters have a poison proc on their attacks.
  collect 6246 quest 1458.1           -- Hatefury Claw
  collect 6247 quest 1458.2           -- Hatefury Horn

step Kreldig Ungor
  turnin 1458
  accept 1459

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Desolace: the west

step Nijel's Point
  zone Desolace
  turnin 1465
  accept 1438
  accept 97284                        -- Vahlarriel Demonslayer: the Burning Blade in Thunder Axe Fortress, where her search leads
  accept 1387                         -- Corporal Melkins: the Kolkar are at the end of this guide
  accept 93224                        -- Captain Pentigast, beside Corporal Melkins

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Thunder Axe Fortress

step Azore Aldamort
  tip Azore's tower stands on the hill west of Thunder Axe Fortress: take his quest first, the sceptre he wants is in the fortress.
  accept 5741

step Karnitol's Chest
  tip The wrecked ship lies just south-west of Azore's tower; its chest sits beside Rackmore's Log.
  turnin 1454                         -- Karnitol's Chest
  accept 1455                         -- For Kreldig Ungor, at the end of this guide
  accept 6161 object 177787           -- Rackmore's Log, beside the chest: its two keys drop only while you have the quest

step Rackmore's Silver Key
  tip West to the shore: the Drysnap Crawlers and Pincers (33-35) on the beach and the clam beds around the wreck carry Rackmore's Silver Key, about one in seven.
  collect 15878 quest 6161.1 @33.4,30.1 map 1443 -- Rackmore's Silver Key, from the Drysnap crabs

step Sar'theris Strand
  tip Keep north to Sar'theris Strand for Rackmore's Golden Key: any Slitherblade can drop it. Work the Naga, Sorceresses and Warriors (32-34) of the strand's southern half until it drops.
  tip Careful: the Myrmidons (34-35) hold the beach's northern half with the Sea Witches and Oracles (34-36, casters), and Tidehunters (36-37) swim off the northern tip: on the way to the chest, keep to the beach and swim straight across.
  collect 15881 quest 6161.2          -- Rackmore's Golden Key, from the Slitherblade naga

step Rackmore's Chest
  tip Swim out to Ranazjar Isle off the far northern tip: Rackmore's Chest stands on the shore beside the Serpent Statue. Open it with both keys; leave the statue alone.
  turnin 6161 @30.0,8.7 map 1443     -- Rackmore's Chest

step Dalinda Malem
  tip Back south-east past Azore's tower to the Burning Blade's fortress: Dalinda hides inside it.
  turnin 1438                         -- Inside
  accept 1439

step Tyranis and the Seer
  tip Her brother Tyranis (36) walks the fortress with the Burning Blade cultists (30-33): pull him alone. The Burning Blade Seer keeps the sceptre in the fortress's main building. Vahlarriel wants four of each kind of cultist on the way.
  collect 6767 quest 1439             -- Tyranis' Pendant; inside
  collect 15750 quest 5741            -- Sceptre of Light; on the top floor
  kill 4663 quest 97284.1             -- Burning Blade Augur
  kill 4664 quest 97284.2             -- Burning Blade Reaver
  kill 4665 quest 97284.3             -- Burning Blade Adept
  kill 4666 quest 97284.4             -- Burning Blade Felsworn

step Escort Dalinda
  turnin 1439                         -- Dalinda Malem, inside
  accept 1440
  goto 58.3,30.9 "Out of Thunder Axe Fortress"
  note Lead Dalinda out of the fortress; she walks off once you are clear of it. Vahlarriel takes the turn-in at Nijel's Point at the end of the guide.
  complete 1440

step Azore Aldamort
  tip Back west up the hill to Azore's tower with the sceptre, then south along the road to Kormek's Hut.
  turnin 5741                         -- Azore Aldamort
  accept 6027                         -- Azore Aldamort: Lord Kragaru (38) rises at the Serpent Statue, for the south loop at the end of 30-40 (06b): keep it

step Bibbly F'utzbuckle
  tip Kormek's Hut stands by the road south of the fortress, on the way to Smeed's camp. Bibbly collects Kodo Bones; they lie among the skeletons of the Kodo Graveyard, where Smeed's kodos are.
  accept 5501

step Smeed Scrabblescrew
  tip Smeed's camp is on the road south of Kolkar Village, by the Kodo Graveyard.
  accept 5561

step Kodo Bones
  tip West into the Kodo Graveyard first: Bibbly's Kodo Bones lie among the skeletons on its western side. Just north of them an Extinguished Campfire starts Highway Robbery, also for Bibbly.
  collect 13703 quest 5501 @47.5,58.5 map 1443 -- Kodo Bone, among the skeletons
  accept 79229 object 417353 @47.46,54.55 map 1443 -- Highway Robbery: the Extinguished Campfire

step Kodo Graveyard
  tip Use Smeed's Kodo Kombobulator on an Aged, Dying or Ancient Kodo: it becomes a tamed kodo that follows you. Walk it back to Smeed's camp; there, talk to the kodo: that counts it and lets you tame the next. Five kodos, one at a time. Careful: the Ancient Kodos (36-37) hit hard: tame them, don't fight them.
  use 13892 @51.0,58.5 "Kodo Kombobulator" -- on an Aged, Dying or Ancient Kodo in the graveyard; don't kill it
  talk 4700 quest 5561.1 @60.6,61.6   -- the tamed kodo, at Smeed's camp: talk to it, five times

step Kodo Graveyard: hides and venom
  tip The Aged Kodos in the graveyard drop the hides, and the Scorpashi Lashers that hunt around it carry the venom. Careful: the Ancient Kodos (36-37) hit hard: fight only the Aged Kodos.
  collect 6249 quest 1459.2
  collect 6248 quest 1459.1           -- Scorpashi Venom

step Smeed Scrabblescrew
  turnin 5561

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Kolkar

step Kolkar Village
  tip North-east from Smeed's camp to Kolkar Village, on the way back to Nijel's Point: every Kolkar drops Centaur Ears for Corporal Melkins and Carved Centaur Totems for Captain Pentigast. The Magram south-east of Smeed's camp drop them too, but their village holds Necromancers (42-43) and Guardians (39-41): stay with the Kolkar (30-35).
  loop
  goto 71.5,45.5 map 1443 era r 110
  goto 71.7,41.6 map 1443 era r 120
  collect 6067 quest 1387 -- Centaur Ear
  collect 254432 quest 93224.1 -- Carved Centaur Totem

step Kormek's Hut
  tip North-west from Kolkar Village back along the road to Nijel's Point: Bibbly waits at Kormek's Hut. He sends you after the robber to Booty Bay, where the next guide ends: keep it.
  turnin 5501                         -- Bibbly F'utzbuckle
  turnin 79229
  accept 79235                        -- Bibbly F'utzbuckle: Tokal waits in Booty Bay, at the end of the next guide

